{"ready":true,"data":{"id":"em-haine","name":"Em Haine","birthDate":"2002-01-25","birthPlace":"Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada","bio":"Emily Haine (born January 25, 2002, in Vancouver, British Columbia) is a Canadian actress who works in film and television. She has a French-Canadian mother and a father who immigrated to Canada from Austria. As a teenager, she was partly home-schooled and later moved to London, England, to study acting, including Meisner training at the Actors Temple. During her stay in London, she was a member of a local punk band called “The Dirt,” where she was active as a bassist and singer.\n\nEm Haine has gradually taken on roles in films and series since around the mid-2010s. Her notable credits include: “Fargo” (FX series, 2015) – her first major television role as Noreen Vanderslice; “Deadpool” (2016) – minor role in the Marvel blockbuster; “Tully” (2018) – Appearance in the Jason Reitman comedy; “Chilling Adventures of Sabrina” (Netflix, 2019) – She played Elspeth in several episodes; “Reginald the Vampire” (Max/Stream, 2022–2024) – She played Sarah Kinney in the series; “Why Can't My Life Be a Rom-Com?” (2023) – Lead role as Eliza Sloane in a romantic TV movie; “Hailey Rose” (2024) – She played the title role of Hailey in the Canadian drama film.\n\nEm Haine is also active on social media, where she shares updates about her career and projects.","source":"TMDB","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T12:42:18+00:00","tmdbId":1602420,"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/person/1602420","credits":[{"id":"deadpool","title":"Deadpool","character":"Whisper Girlfriend"}],"photo":"./public-data/images/people/em-haine.webp","filmography":[{"name":"Hailey Rose","year":2024,"character":"Hailey","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/igaM66WEPtiEjq39ka4n6FNuwqa.jpg"},{"name":"Why Can't My Life Be a Rom-Com?","year":2023,"character":"Eliza Sloane","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/e9l5Tg3rLwBXqvWRaTC3aRmfXhc.